# tests/ is published on purpose: README.md and AGENTS.public.md both tell an
# external reader how to run it. tests/internal/ stays behind, because those
# assertions read files that exist only in the repository this tool is
# developed in.
tests/internal/ export-ignore

# Internal agent context — kept out of the public mirror. The participant-facing
# equivalents are AGENTS.public.md / CLAUDE.public.md, renamed on publish. The
# split exists because the internal copy describes tests/internal/ and the CI
# that runs this tool, neither of which a reader of the published copy has.
/AGENTS.md export-ignore
